<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>OpenAI cancels release of new artificial intelligence model over safety concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07fb24bd291c863f9838d6cce621e8ebfac77c54693e284ca83e3ff5bf0e02d8</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T02:54:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-openai-cancels-release-new-ai-model-safety-concerns--342610ada246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-openai-cancels-release-new-ai-model-safety-concerns" /><summary type="html">OpenAI will not release its latest artificial intelligence model, Astra 6.1, after internal tests found it fell short of safety standards, the maker of ChatGPT confirmed on Monday. The decision came ahead of a meeting of AI leaders at the White House Tuesday convened by US President Donald Trump and House Speaker Mike Johnson amid mounting controversy over the risks posed by rogue AI.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Argentina’s Milei threatens to sue UK over Falkland Islands oil project</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf0e517edbc688ad8c6c85747eea0722d67c18547dce32987c410a608f24783</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T02:13:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-argentina-milei-arbitration-falklands-oil-project--6c7f62fb9112.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-argentina-milei-arbitration-falklands-oil-project" /><summary type="html">Argentine President Javier Milei on Monday threatened to sue the UK over the Sea Lion oil project near the disputed Falkland Islands. Argentina claims sovereignty over the British-administered territory, where a 1982 war killed 255 British and 649 Argentine troops. Developers Navitas and Rockhopper say they hold valid British-issued exploration licences.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US prosecutors reopen Cornell university gang rape investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e74048cc841b816d9f457b712fe2af1f097358b6e4ec802ec47132eb966a8af</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T00:04:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-prosecutors-cornell-university-gang-rape-investigation--ba1abd3dd231.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-prosecutors-cornell-university-gang-rape-investigation" /><summary type="html">US prosecutors reopened an investigation on Monday into an alleged 2024 gang rape at Cornell University after the woman involved accused the school of failing to punish those responsible adequately. In a lawsuit, she said seven Chi Phi fraternity members had drugged her with ketamine and assaulted her.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US deportations are triggering a 'cascade' of rights abuses, UN experts warn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b34de2f2c1b1d72dbf53790dcb61884ae156baa606274e90b26a1a268949f2a7</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:01:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260928-us-trump-deportations-triggering-cascade-of-rights-abuses-un-experts-warn-forbidden-stories--010f924e89a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260928-us-trump-deportations-triggering-cascade-of-rights-abuses-un-experts-warn-forbidden-stories" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration's policy of deportating thousands of people to countries with which they have no links is "increasing risks of torture and ill-treatment and enforced disappearance", a panel of independent UN experts warned on Monday. An investigation by an international consortium of journalists including FRANCE 24 reporters determined last week that more than 25,000 third-country nationals had been deported by the end of August.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Great Black Hope: Pursuit of belonging 'becomes a kind of cancer that eats them from the inside out'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b08070b7a5565f476335a525ed14421247294fa4a701298498498ab2b73c15c</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:37:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out--ca6f07533dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome award-winning author Rob Franklin, joining us to discuss Great Black Hope, his acclaimed debut novel exploring race, class, respectability and belonging. Franklin wanted to write about the worlds he had spent years observing since childhood: including how class and race shape even our most intimate relationships.  At its centre is David Smith, a young Black man from a Southern bourgeois family. His education, manners and connections give him access, but he is constantly aware of the possibility of being cast out. That tension led him to think about respectability politics and the psychological cost of constantly performing an acceptable version of oneself.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Trump hosts Xi, the pope visits France and floods ravage Thailand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63c9a8c854997864a2e26568c914ecc95057d821155fa730152105312e4d1274</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:05:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260927-the-week-in-pictures-trump-hosts-xi-the-pope-visits-france-and-floods-ravage-thailand--94b87d455e05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260927-the-week-in-pictures-trump-hosts-xi-the-pope-visits-france-and-floods-ravage-thailand" /><summary type="html">From Pope Leo XIV's historic first visit to France to US President Donald Trump meeting China's President Xi Jinping to flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Unusually powerful storm pummels northeast US with heavy rain, high winds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:839c964c61e6844a143fdb34a96e43d795ae45ba9514633dda9a8052f1a695d1</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:08:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-unusually-powerful-storm-pummels-northeast-us-with-heavy-rain-high-winds--c49e19e43688.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-unusually-powerful-storm-pummels-northeast-us-with-heavy-rain-high-winds" /><summary type="html">A powerful storm unusual for this time of year intensified on Sunday over the northeastern United States, bringing torrential rain and powerful winds that cut off power to tens of thousands of people and killed one person, according to US media.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's President Lula bans online betting ahead of presidential election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d6e71ee6feb347f4baa9a7d2051407387a23e1f2528b255a7cae09c223a8b53</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:36:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election--48f3127e0de1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva on Friday signed an order banning fixed-odds betting just over a week ahead of the first round of the presidential election, in a move he said was designed to tackle the pervasive problem of families falling into debt.</summary></entry><entry><title>CNN removed from Trump press pool despite judge order to reinstate White House access</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4285ae00456a4ab2a05d723209a3d3392a057f6c193e2c55f8ce6597f78ef34</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T05:56:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-cnn-removed-from-trump-press-pool-despite-judge-order-to-reinstate-white-house-access--0156d346bb62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-cnn-removed-from-trump-press-pool-despite-judge-order-to-reinstate-white-house-access" /><summary type="html">US news outlet CNN has been removed from a press pool that is accompanying President Donald Trump on a trip to Tennessee on Saturday. Last week, the Trump administration barred CNN, along with MS NOW and Politico, from accessing the White House. A judge then ordered their access temporarily restored, saying the move was likely unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lots of pomp but little progress as Trump and Xi end state visit to DC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f3c3acf4691b85573a870f4135ceab90f04d7e91442146d47a08ad51b05e3b4</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:58:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit--18a60b896000.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and Chinese leader Xi Jinping capped a state visit to Washington on Friday with pomp and pageantry but no real breakthroughs. Trump said he discussed the Iran war with Xi during his two-day visit, with both men confirming they will meet twice more before the end of the year.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court allows Trump to use controversial voter 'verification' system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16029a08db055298a15ef0c3fb8e61b06abdd980c6cd31f783c10dcc3d311355</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry--2eef72391964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Friday ruled the Trump administration can use a controversial new federal database that would ostensibly verify voter citizenship in November’s elections. Critics argue the administration is exaggerating the threat of non-citizen voters – an extreme rarity in US elections – to implement policies that would disenfranchise likely Democratic voters.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump courts Xi Jinping during high-profile White House visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8d5dd77cba58d4261fd9f09df4fa2736e6517735db7b3606ac58a3c26b7040f</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:38:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit--c7b3bc8b15d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump rolled out an unusually lavish welcome for Chinese President Xi Jinping, praising their personal friendship throughout a White House state dinner and other ceremonial events. While both leaders said they held frank discussions behind closed doors, the visit produced no major breakthroughs, prompting criticism from Democratic lawmakers who argued the pageantry overshadowed pressing issues including Iran, Taiwan, AI and trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentina's poverty rate climbs to nearly one in three under Milei</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23055d2de952dcbb8b7e586437ad25948bef5713b9fa6ea1f5301db3a09985c0</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T02:30:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei--169ea5474e26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei" /><summary type="html">Argentina’s poverty rate rose to 32.3% in the first half of 2026 from 28.2% in the previous six months, official data showed on Thursday, as incomes lagged rising prices. Extreme poverty climbed to 7.5% from 6.3%. Among children aged 14 and under, 44.5% were poor.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Send in the Clowns': Viral video fuels claims Denmark trolled Trump and Rubio</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70ca2a7ecf5b334757b89ae2a1f744f53e8e278f1cd08159fb128a9a89b97b29</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T21:00:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1--4ceb91c9c0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1" /><summary type="html">A viral video claims Danish officials played Judy Collins's "Send in the Clowns" as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio arrived for a Greenland signing ceremony, sparking claims of Danish "trolling". Our checks of separate livestreams confirm the song really played and the video was not manipulated. Denmark has denied choosing the music, while the UN says it did not organise the event. Whilst the song was real, there is no evidence Denmark selected it deliberately. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli policies threaten 'life and existence' of Palestinians, Abbas tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:526f554340c1cb57cd79db893f9fc600d9803dbc8868847c844dba866a723cee</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un--ab406195501e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday by video after being denied a visa to the United States for the second year in a row. In his prerecorded speech, he denounced Israeli policies that he said threatened Palestinians with a new Nakba and vowed that his people would remain “on their land”.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc7d45d940685bef5ff371244af3b248b30ffa01723e972f15ff9a69978a3c58</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Does the future belong to China?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f677c9504884dab414e2ee1fa4676cf50421bd8ba6fc4570c64530e472f4824</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:32:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china--300d0d1807be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump is rolling out the red carpet for his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping ahead of Thursday's summit in Washington. But is China's leader overconfident in thinking the future belongs to Beijing? FRANCE 24's Yinka Oyetade speaks to Rex Li from King's College London.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump startled by the sound of a fighter jet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bf7f65c039cde114919ea3782009cb6e057e1d4bd33181a2d623299bbba1d5b</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:03:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet--fd5a564dc607.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 As Donald #Trump welcomed his Chinese counterpart Xi #Jinping for a state visit on the tarmac of an airport near #Washington, the sound of a fighter jet during the military ceremony caught the US president off guard, prompting a series of startled facial expressions.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Death of the Soccer God' pays 'homage' to Haitian diaspora and 'those who go back &amp; do their best'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678ad09703595069be04ef1a31848bf681474cb159ba0d227ad573a461743bf9</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T06:29:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/death-of-the-soccer-god-pays-homage-to-haitian-diaspora-and-those-who-go-back-do-their-best--5ffff12e809e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/death-of-the-soccer-god-pays-homage-to-haitian-diaspora-and-those-who-go-back-do-their-best" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Dimitry Elias Léger, journalist and author of "Death of the Soccer God". He begins with an extraordinary but largely forgotten moment in sporting history: the Haitian-born Joe Gaetjens scoring the goal that gave the US its famous victory over England at the 1950 World Cup. But Léger is less interested in reconstructing Gaetjens’s biography than in using the football star's journey as a " jumping point" to examining diaspora, fame, mortality and moral responsibility. Success offers neither immunity from history nor escape from mortality: as he puts it, “You could be super famous and end up on death row” or die wealthy in your own bed: “Either way, you’re going to die.</summary></entry><entry><title>Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW return to White House hours after judge reorders Trump to lift ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17a99a7aa7d5e49077a49c6ae1277d76adf6224934dbf5275a11779af9d6692b</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T05:31:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico--9468ed6cf08e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico" /><summary type="html">Reporters from ​Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW were allowed to enter the ​White ‌House ⁠on ‌Thursday afternoon after being barred in the morning, despite a US federal judge ordering the reinstatement of their access. The judge then issued a second order for the Trump administration to restore the journalists' access after the media outlets called for an emergency follow-up ⁠hearing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France to send 'military means' to protect key Saudi oil port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7126f44ec3b6f98d709ac72e5df7f71a3b0589248d8836f8b14d850652a7cd3f</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T03:11:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday said his country would send "military means" to protect a Saudi oil terminal from attacks by Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis. Saudi Arabia has been using the Red Sea port of Yanbu to export oil after Iran blockaded the Strait of Hormuz. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump gives Xi rare airport welcome as Chinese leader begins US state visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ad0a3a80cd89ba255ee679bfcead6f0324f2a79b3cd3bd8019d0b200da4a5a0</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T01:48:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-trump-gives-xi-rare-airport-welcome-as-chinese-leader-begins-us-state-visit--890faee8eac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-trump-gives-xi-rare-airport-welcome-as-chinese-leader-begins-us-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump personally welcomed Chinese President Xi Jinping at a military airfield outside Washington on Wednesday, kicking off a lavish state visit focused on trade, artificial intelligence and Iran, as the two powers seek to preserve a fragile diplomatic and economic truce.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>AI leaders urge caution at UN, with Anthropic chief pledging to slow down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0ad974a1b05a22eee8367c9d8e7807554afc922c961b15fb23cdf8b59fa4030</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T21:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-ai-leaders-urge-caution-at-un-with-anthropic-chief-pledging-to-slow-down--0376a5057ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-ai-leaders-urge-caution-at-un-with-anthropic-chief-pledging-to-slow-down" /><summary type="html">Leaders of some of the world's biggest AI companies urged caution at the United Nations on Wednesday, warning that increasingly autonomous systems could outpace human oversight. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei pledged to slow development to ensure new AI systems are safe, while OpenAI chief Sam Altman called for "extreme care".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fact-checking Trump's speech at the United Nations General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e656420f47437a54c4e49d163bac878d57578fe9116e25b21f9962f6dfa7978</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T20:54:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fact-checking-trump-s-speech-at-the-united-nations-general-assembly-1--90883f567137.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fact-checking-trump-s-speech-at-the-united-nations-general-assembly-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's UN address was packed with claims that are misleading, false or exaggerated. He said the US has more munitions than it could ever use, despite reports of depleting stocks. He also claimed the US and Venezuela hold 60 percent of the world's oil, despite the numbers not adding up, and he said he had ended the war in Gaza despite ongoing Israeli strikes and deaths since last year's ceasefire. Vedika Bahl fact-checks the speech in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>No, this video doesn't disprove the 9/11 attack on the south tower of the World Trade Center</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea04bf11708af00b87543995377246a38ec533d2b6f3adf4ed9fb4a93ea03cd1</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:01:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11--3315503e2a84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11" /><summary type="html">A former British member of parliament implied that a video filmed from a helicopter on September 11, 2001 shows that no planes actually hit the World Trade Center's south tower, but this claim would be unfounded. The plane that hit the south tower hit the other side of the building, which isn’t visible in the video.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Disgraced Hollywood mogul Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab054c5e375697961c9c1bdf0c2eb8cf726a14fbf3c07a1718070380f6df209b</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /><summary type="html">Disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday in another #MeToo reckoning for sexually assaulting a former production assistant in 2006.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US says wants Ukraine, Russia to end strikes on energy sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f6259e7cdccf22e478c05503834e4ed49a88d9343ffbc753f3a096f05ffa70</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1--6a47cb7c5c74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to address the UN General Assembly on Wednesday, as US President Donald Trump pushes for an end to Russia’s war and Kyiv seeks to shape renewed diplomatic efforts after more than four and a half years of conflict. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy set to address UN as Russia strikes Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f79c0b99b0446709e5324f62409c9f6cc94dd96b58bbd4ac69209f6c3585b40</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1--602f8dc2d515.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukraine’s capital, Kyiv, with drones in daylight attacks on Wednesday, killing two people and wounding 23, just hours before Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy was due to address world leaders at the UN General Assembly. Zelenskyy met US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, as Trump has expressed frustration over the lack of progress in talks aimed at ending the war and the continued escalation of aerial attacks by both sides. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b07d9a21cc839eb674830c04a8d9669fbc4644073e74de87e955514bf3f814</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:401d049d325012f0ffcb9c0a49e8c2a32d9d63a90ed7a68621b03f3f5b103ffd</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry></feed>
